man-Add-ADPrincipalGroupMembership = adds an account to groups: the same as Add-ADGroupMember, seen from the account.
    .synopsis = Add-ADPrincipalGroupMembership [-Identity] <Object> [-MemberOf] <Object[]> [-PassThru]
    .option-Identity = the account: its DN, GUID, SID or sAMAccountName (or objects from the pipeline).
    .option-MemberOf = the groups to join.
    .option-PassThru = return the account.
    .example-1 = eve joins a group
man-Remove-ADPrincipalGroupMembership = removes an account from groups (it asks first). Its primary group (Domain Users) can't be removed this way.
    .synopsis = Remove-ADPrincipalGroupMembership [-Identity] <Object> [-MemberOf] <Object[]> [-Confirm]
    .option-Identity = the account: its DN, GUID, SID or sAMAccountName (or objects from the pipeline).
    .option-MemberOf = the groups to leave.
    .example-1 = without the question
man-New-ADOrganizationalUnit = creates an organizational unit (under the domain by default), protected from accidental deletion unless told otherwise. OUs are where GPOs are linked and where administration is delegated.
    .synopsis = New-ADOrganizationalUnit [-Name] <String> [-Path <String>] [-Description <String>] [-ProtectedFromAccidentalDeletion <Boolean>] [-PassThru]
