man-Get-ADDomainController = gets a domain controller: its host name, address, site, roles (OperationMasterRoles), global catalog.
    .synopsis = Get-ADDomainController [[-Identity] <Object>] [-Discover]
    .option-Identity = the object: its DN, GUID, SID or sAMAccountName (or objects from the pipeline).
    .option-Discover = find one (here: the only one).
    .example-1 = which server answers
man-Get-ADDefaultDomainPasswordPolicy = gets the domain's password and lockout policy: MinPasswordLength, MaxPasswordAge, ComplexityEnabled, PasswordHistoryCount, LockoutThreshold (0: never locks, the default), LockoutDuration, LockoutObservationWindow (after it, the count of bad passwords starts again).
    .synopsis = Get-ADDefaultDomainPasswordPolicy [[-Identity] <Object>]
    .option-Identity = the object: its DN, GUID, SID or sAMAccountName (or objects from the pipeline).
    .example-1 = the rules every account follows
man-Set-ADDefaultDomainPasswordPolicy = changes the domain's password and lockout policy (kept in the Default Domain Policy too).
    .synopsis = Set-ADDefaultDomainPasswordPolicy [-Identity] <Object> [-LockoutThreshold <Int32>] [-LockoutDuration <TimeSpan>] [-LockoutObservationWindow <TimeSpan>] [-MinPasswordLength <Int32>] [-ComplexityEnabled <Boolean>] [-MaxPasswordAge <TimeSpan>]
