man-Get-GPO = gets Group Policy objects: DisplayName, Id, GpoStatus (AllSettingsEnabled, UserSettingsDisabled…), owner, dates, versions.
    .synopsis = Get-GPO [-Name] <String> | -Guid <Guid> | -All
    .option-Name = the GPO by its name.
    .option-Guid = the GPO by its id.
    .option-All = every GPO of the domain.
    .example-1 = the domain's GPOs
    .example-2 = one GPO
man-New-GPO = creates an empty GPO (link it with New-GPLink; Authenticated Users apply it by default).
    .synopsis = New-GPO [-Name] <String> [-Comment <String>]
    .option-Name = its name.
    .option-Comment = its description.
    .example-1 = created and linked at once
man-Remove-GPO = deletes a GPO and its links.
    .synopsis = Remove-GPO [-Name] <String> | -Guid <Guid>
    .option-Name = the GPO by its name.
    .option-Guid = the GPO by its id.
    .example-1 = what would go
man-New-GPLink = links a GPO to the domain or an OU: the users and computers below get it (Domain, then each OU down; the closest wins, link order 1 inside a container).
